//// The spelling that has no answer (the other half of `run/variant_name_collision.bp`).
////
//// `Circle` is a variant of `Shape` and a variant of `Hole`, and `.Circle`
//// bound with no annotation says which of the two only if something at the
//// site does — and nothing here does. The checker refuses it for every target
//// (01 step 12, decision 67); until then only the erlang emitter refused, and
//// erlang before it tagged the value with one of the two and died at a `case`
//// with `{case_clause, …Shape__v__circle}`. Where the position does say — a
//// typed parameter, an annotation — `.Circle` is that enum's
//// (`run/variant_leading_dot_expected.bp`).

pub type Shape {
    Circle,
    Square,
}

pub type Hole {
    Circle,
    Slot,
}

pub fn main() {
    val c = .Circle;
    @print(0);
}
